      "writtenOn": "2022-02-21T17:07:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The problem with reducing the dataLimit is that I have to increase the time the test runs, so it doesn\u0027t become flaky. On my Pixel 4a, I get ~60MB/s here.\n\n--\nI tried reducing this to 1MB/s, which caused the test to break on cuttlefish (but passed fine on sunfish; weird). Increasing it to 10s (tried 5s and 8s, both were flaky on cf) fixes it, but then that makes this test take forever.\n\nI want to investigate a little more on why that is the case, a burst size of 128KiB does not solely explain the results I am seeing. I have little knowledge of how act_police actually works / counts data (does it count the protocol headers?).",
